<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14853" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ductĭto</span></b> , āvi,
			v. freq. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to lead</i>, <i>to lead with one</i> (a Plautin.
			word). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen., <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud.
				2, 7, 26</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In partic., <i>to lead home</i> a wife, <i>to marry</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Poen. 1, 2, 60</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to deceive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ego follitim ductitabo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Epid. 3, 2, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
